## 4. Minecraft account verification

A major problem is that someone could register another player’s username.

You have three possible verification levels.

### Basic

The user enters their username with no ownership verification.

Good for a small friend group.

### Discord verification

Require users to join your Discord and connect their Discord account.

```text
Discord: kaikub#1234
Minecraft: kaikub
```

An admin approves the connection.

### In-game verification

Best for more serious servers.

The website generates a code:

```text
Verification code: CEDT-4821
```

The player temporarily joins a verification server or uses a Discord bot command:

```text
/verify CEDT-4821
```

For your private 30-player server, Discord login plus admin approval is probably enough.

